  "description": "Historical events. Kinds: (a) initial_war — conflicts in progress on 1836-01-01, part of the starting state in BOTH modes; (b) exogenous — natural or biological shocks. Historical Mode fires them on the recorded date (their severity is computed by the shared simulation from the current state); Sandbox Mode uses the stochastic analogue named in 'sandbox_analogue' with the same mechanics; (c) decision_window — HISTORICAL MODE ONLY: during the window, if all conditions hold in the simulated world, the AI of the entity is offered the choice and weights the historical option more heavily. Nothing is forced: if conditions never hold, the window simply passes. (d) structural_rule — legal facts that apply in both modes (e.g. Salic law in Hanover).",
